# Changelog — host companion

## Unreleased

- fix (H2): the daemon no longer aborts at its heap limit when a few long permission prompts wait during heavy subagent activity. The long-poll buffer keeps each change serialized once and is capped at 2 M characters as well as 1000 changes (an older cursor gets a snapshot, as after a restart); the old-space limit is 64 MB instead of 16 (a ceiling: idle RSS is unchanged); the daemon's stderr goes to `hostd.log`, so a fatal V8 error leaves a trace; any exit that still runs JS removes `hostd.pid`.
- fix (M17): a stale `hostd.pid` whose pid now belongs to another process (after a reboot or a crash) no longer blocks the daemon. The daemon sets its process title to `conductore-hostd`; the sh clients check `/proc/<pid>/comm` besides `kill -0`, and the daemon checks the command line (`ps` without `/proc`) before it gives up the lock.
- fix (M19): the socket is always `~/.conductore/hostd.sock`, beside the lock, instead of depending on the starter's `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` (a tmux server started from cron or su made `events` fail and `status` serve a stale snapshot). The CLI still reaches (and `install` still stops) a 0.7 daemon listening in `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/conductore`.
- fix (M20): agents that never send SessionEnd (Claude Code killed, crashed, SSH dropped, a reboot) no longer stay forever. The hook passes Claude Code's pid (`claude_pid`, its parent or grandparent through `sh -c`, read from `/proc` without a fork); the daemon records it with its start time as `process` when it is Claude Code and ends the agent (`reason: expired`) once it is gone, checked at start and on `status` / `events`. Without `/proc`, an agent ends after 24 h without an event.
- fix (M18): the prompt relay (`send`, `interrupt`, `focus`) can no longer type into the wrong pane. Agents' `tmux` records carry the server `socket` (from `$TMUX`) and the `panePid`; every tmux command goes to that server (`-S`), and right before typing the pane must still run that process, a Herdr pane must still run this Claude session (`herdr pane list`), and Claude Code must still run. Otherwise nothing is typed and the error says why. Records from older daemons are refused until the agent's next event.
- fix (M22): `install` / `uninstall` rewrite `~/.claude/settings.json` through its symlink (a dotfiles link stays a link and its target is updated) and keep the file's mode, 0600 when new, instead of the process umask (a 0600 file holding an API key became 0644).
- fix (L18): a PermissionRequest spool file over 8 MB is answered at once (the terminal asks) instead of leaving its hook waiting the full timeout; the daemon reads only its header and logs the drop. An unparseable one already was.

## 0.7.0 (2026-09-25)

- feat: `summarize [--max-words 45] [--timeout-ms 20000]`: a one- or two-sentence spoken version of the reply on stdin (64 KB max) for the phone's "Claude summary" read-aloud mode, as one JSON line (`summary`, `ms`, `model`, or `error`: claude-missing, not-logged-in, timeout, busy, failed; exit 0). Replies under 40 words come back as they are (`passthrough: true`) without calling Claude.
- It runs `claude -p --tools "" --safe-mode --no-session-persistence --output-format json --model haiku` with a fixed system prompt and the reply on stdin between random delimiters: no tools, no hooks (never seen as an agent), no transcript. Thinking is off (`MAX_THINKING_TOKENS=0`): about 3 s per call instead of 5–55 s. Nice 10, its own process group killed on timeout, one call per user at a time, the text never logged or stored. A CLI one-shot: no daemon change, nothing at idle.
- The phone's other commands are unchanged; older phones never call `summarize`.

## 0.6.0 (2026-09-25)

- feat: `usage [--days 7] [--since <iso>]`: usage at a glance, computed on the host from local files. Claude's 5-hour and 7-day limits (newest statusline reports, remembered after the sessions end), context per live session, and tokens with an estimated cost per local day, project and model from the Claude Code transcripts (`~/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl`, each message counted once); Codex CLI tokens and rate limits from `~/.codex/sessions` when present (`codex.present: false` otherwise). Costs come from one dated price table (`lib/pricing.js`) and are labelled an estimate (API-equivalent on subscription plans).
- perf: the scan is incremental (per-file offsets and daily sums in `~/.conductore/usage-cache.json`, last 31 days), capped per call (`--max-bytes` 256 MB, `--max-ms` 2500, then `scan.partial: true`), runs at nice 10 and never involves the daemon's event path. On a machine with 1,137 transcripts (2 GB in 31 days) the first fill takes five calls of 0.5–0.9 s; later calls take ~60 ms.
- The phone's other commands are unchanged; older phones never call `usage`.

## 0.5.0 (2026-09-25)

- feat: `ports [--since <seq>]` lists the TCP ports the user's own processes listen on (dev servers), with process, `label` (vite, next, …), cwd and the `seq` at which each first appeared, for the phone's "Preview ready" chip. Computed on request from `ss -ltnpH` (else `lsof`, else `/proc/net/tcp`), reused for 2 s, remembered in `~/.conductore/ports.json`; system ports and daemons are left out. No daemon change; older phones never call it.

## 0.4.0 (2026-09-25)

- perf: the hook (`conductore-hook`) and the statusline (new `conductore-statusline`) are POSIX sh scripts: no Node start per event. An event is spooled as one file (`cat` + `ln`) in `~/.conductore/spool`, which the daemon watches; 2.4 ms and 1.9 MB peak per event instead of 34 ms and 46 MB. PermissionRequest waits on a FIFO the daemon answers (same decision JSON, same "always" rules, same timeout behaviour).
- perf: statusline reports wake the daemon at most once per 10 s per session (hold + parked reports, the last value is never lost); the default line is built without Node.
- perf: daemon diet: `--max-old-space-size=16 --max-semi-space-size=1 --lite-mode --v8-pool-size=1` (4 threads instead of 7, 47 MB RSS / 7.4 MB private instead of 54 / 8.8), no periodic timers (the 5 min prune interval is now a one-shot at the next deadline), snapshot debounce 1 s, per-event log lines only with `CONDUCTORE_LOG=debug`, idle exit after 6 h (`CONDUCTORE_IDLE_EXIT_S`).
- feat: tmux location is resolved by the daemon (cached 5 s per pane); `install` records the node path for the sh clients and migrates 0.3 settings (Node hook entries, `conductore-hostd statusline --chain`); `doctor` reports hook latency and daemon memory; `host/bench.sh`.
- fix: a starting daemon never takes over a socket another live daemon serves, and a custom `CONDUCTORE_HOME` keeps its socket inside it (a test daemon could unlink the real one).
- fix: agents in Herdr get `herdr.workspaceId` / `tabId` / `paneId` from Herdr even when the hook's environment lacks some `HERDR_*` variables (one cached `herdr pane list` in the daemon, matched by pane id or Claude session id); the cwd is never a location.
- The phone's CLI contract (`status`, `events`, `transcript`, `send`, `interrupt`, `decide`, `focus`, `version`, `doctor`) is unchanged; `status` now also applies events still waiting in the spool.

## 0.3.0 (2026-09-25)

- feat: `statusline [--chain '<cmd>']` records context and rate-limit usage per session (`usage` on each agent, throttled `reason: usage` changes); `install` wires or wraps `statusLine`, `uninstall` restores it, `doctor` reports it.

## 0.2.0 (2026-09-25)

- feat: chat view support: agents carry `transcriptPath`; new `transcript` (incremental, capped JSONL reader with `--since` / `--before` / `--tail-bytes`), `send` (types a prompt into the agent's Herdr or tmux pane, no shell) and `interrupt` (Escape) commands.
- fix: agent names drop the status glyphs Claude Code puts in the terminal title ("⚠ claude", "✳ Fix tests"); a bare "claude" window name falls back to the cwd basename.

## 0.1.0 (2026-09-24)

- feat: conductore-hostd daemon + conductore-hook client: Claude Code hook events -> per-agent state over a unix socket, `status` / `events` long-poll / `decide` / `focus` / `install` / `uninstall` / `doctor` / `stop` CLI for the phone, PermissionRequest answered from the phone (allow / deny / always). Replaces moshi-hook.
